## Profiles (4)

Default: `max-breaker`.

| Profile        | Route priority (high → low)        | Lower-priority routes |
|----------------|------------------------------------|------------------------|
| `max-breaker`  | all 8 routes active, no priority  | (none)                 |
| `builder`      | CODE, EXEC, RESEARCH, CREATIVE    | PENTEST, GAME, REVERSE, NETWORK |
| `research`     | RESEARCH, REVERSE, NETWORK, CODE  | CREATIVE               |
| `creative`     | CREATIVE, RESEARCH, CODE          | PENTEST, GAME, REVERSE, NETWORK |

A "lower-priority route" still routes the request when the user explicitly forces it (`[ROUTE] prefix`) or when no higher-priority route covers the topic. The list is tiebreak priority, not a veto.

Switch with `[[AX:PROFILE=X]]` (see Control commands below).

